KG42.register("nodes-fa2f9c6b5fe9ccfed829a8b6",{"id":"COMP-ae4944a1a62bf858","code":"EXE024","label":"Interface between bilateral trades and upstream exchange within operating envelopes","definition":"Under LMO coordination, buyers and sellers conduct transactions according to the bilaterally optimized quantities and P2P prices; after P2P transactions, the remaining imports and exports may be traded with the upstream grid within the DOE. When there is no P2P transaction, the strategy assumes that the grid-side transaction quantity equals the allocated DOE.","layer":"L7","template_code":"BCT","concept_id":"execution.energy_trade","concept_ids":["execution.energy_trade"],"identity_dimensions":{"identity_fields":["Object: bilateral P2P exchange and residual grid-side exchange","Core operation: execute buying and selling and connect the residual imports and exports to upstream trading","Output: bilateral exchange conducted according to quantity and price and conditional grid-side uptake"]},"exclusions":["Execution complies with quantity declaration, binary transaction status, and the DOE boundary","Import branch P̂>0, the purchased quantity is non-negative, and the combined peer and grid-side amount does not exceed P̂","Export branch P̂≤0, the sales quantity is non-positive, and the combined peer and grid-side amount is not less than P̂","The P2P aggregate balance and the pairwise P^{pb}_{j,i,t}+P^{ps}_{i,j,t}=0 are execution conditions","The example allows a buyer to trade simultaneously with multiple sellers, and vice versa","The equality of grid-side transactions to DOE when there is no P2P is a source assumption"],"members":[{"id":"43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R006::V::execution.energy_trade","rule_id":"v141-c-R006","market_meaning":"The submitted total P2P buying-quantity bid limits each individual P2P purchase through the upper bound P^{pb}_{j,t} C_{j,i,t}. Scope: Individual P2P purchases by prosumer j from a different prosumer i at each time t. Condition: Subject to the trading-status factor C_{j,i,t} in (36). The submitted total P2P selling-quantity bid limits each individual P2P sale through the signed lower bound P^{ps}_{j,t}(1 − C_{j,i,t}). Scope: Individual P2P sales by prosumer j to a different prosumer i at each time t. Condition: Subject to the complementary trading-status factor 1 − C_{j,i,t} in (37); selling quantities are nonpositive. The local market operator executes and coordinates P2P trading among prosumers. Scope: The proposed LEM's P2P trading process, including Step 9. The optimal P2P trading price applies to the executed exchange between a buyer and a seller. Scope: P2P exchanges reported in Fig. 12 at the sample time t=39. Combined peer and upstream-grid purchases must not exceed the assigned import DOE. Each peer and grid buying quantity is nonnegative and individually bounded by that DOE. Scope: Prosumer purchases from peers and the upstream grid in each time-slot. Condition: The assigned DOE P̂_{j,t} is positive. Combined signed peer and upstream-grid sales must be at or above the assigned export DOE. Each peer and grid selling quantity lies between that DOE and zero. Scope: Prosumer sales to peers and the upstream grid in each time-slot, using nonpositive signed selling quantities. Condition: The assigned DOE P̂_{j,t} is nonpositive. Total P2P buying and total P2P selling must balance in each time-slot. Scope: Aggregate P2P trading in each time-slot τ. The amount bought by j from i must equal the amount sold by i to j in the same trade and time-slot. Scope: Each individual P2P trade between distinct prosumers j and i at time t. Remaining imports or exports may be traded with the upstream grid. Scope: Residual upstream-grid exchanges included in the LEM. Condition: Imports or exports remain after P2P trading and are within the assigned DOE P̂_{j,t}. The strategy assumes that the grid trade equals the assigned DOE. Scope: Upstream-grid trading included in the proposed LEM strategy. Condition: No P2P trade occurs.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"activation","context_text":"Aggregate P2P trading in each time-slot τ. | Each individual P2P trade between distinct prosumers j and i at time t. | Individual P2P purchases by prosumer j from a different prosumer i at each time t. | Individual P2P sales by prosumer j to a different prosumer i at each time t. | P2P exchanges reported in Fig. 12 at the sample time t=39. | Prosumer purchases from peers and the upstream grid in each time-slot. | Prosumer sales to peers and the upstream grid in each time-slot, using nonpositive signed selling quantities. | Residual upstream-grid exchanges included in the LEM. | The proposed LEM's P2P trading process, including Step 9. | Upstream-grid trading included in the proposed LEM strategy.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g02-E27","v141-b-g02-E28","v141-b-g02-E29","v141-b-g02-E30","v141-b-g02-E31","v141-b-g02-E33","v141-b-g02-E34","v141-b-g03-e013","v141-b-g03-e014"]},"constraint_refs":["43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C001","43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C002","43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C003","43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C004","43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C005","43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C006","43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C007","43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C008","43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C009","43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C010"],"decision_anchor":"execution.energy_trade","source_rule_sha256":"6f886284b421760a203dcd266e69537ae7b3451952fb1d55cbec933b14f8be6f","paper":"43-operating_envelope_ev_market","rule_ref":"43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R006","node_id":"execution.energy_trade","function":"execution.energy_trade","unit_id":"43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-a-M03-lem::execution.energy_trade","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M03-lem","anchor":true}],"paper_ids":["43-operating_envelope_ev_market"],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E27","location":{"location_id":"src-1fe7e180ad-p07-c2r1__v141-a-M03-bidding","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"Prosumers Bidding Strategy","anchor_text":"IEEE TRANSACTIONS ON SMART GRID, VOL. 15, NO. 2, MARCH 2024 lem tou lem ad min Ppbj,t · j,t + Pgbj,t","equation_id":"(28)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Prosumers can decide on their participation in the P2P trading or trading with the upstream grid by generating their bids for buying/selling energy within DOEs. Each prosumer decides on the trading bids and submits them to the LEM in each τ by the proposed bidding strategy. In this case, the objective of prosumer is to minimize the total trading cost as, min ∑_{j∈J} (P^{pb}_{j,t}·Λ^{lem}_{j,t} + P^{gb}_{j,t}·Λ^{tou}_{j,t} + P^{ps}_{j,t}·Λ^{lem}_{j,t} + P^{gs}_{j,t}·Λ^{fit}_{t}) τ; P^{ps}_{j,t}, P^{gs}_{j,t} ≤ 0, ∀j∈J,∀t∈T, subject to: (29)−(35), (28) where the first and second terms in (28) refer to the total cost of buying energy from the peers and the upstream grid, respectively and the third and fourth terms define the total profit of selling energy to the peers and the upstream grid in the LEM, respectively. Here, P^{pb}_{j,t}/P^{ps}_{j,t} and P^{gb}_{j,t}/P^{gs}_{j,t} are buying/selling quantities of prosumer j with the peers and the upstream grid in each τ, respectively; and Λ^{tou}_{j,t} are the time-of-use (ToU) buying prices with the upstream grid.","paper":"43-operating_envelope_ev_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R006","quote":"Prosumers can decide on their participation in the P2P trading or trading with the upstream grid by generating their bids for buying/selling energy within DOEs. Each prosumer decides on the trading bids and submits them to the LEM in each τ by the proposed bidding strategy. In this case, the objective of prosumer is to minimize the total trading cost as, min ∑_{j∈J} (P^{pb}_{j,t}·Λ^{lem}_{j,t} + P^{gb}_{j,t}·Λ^{tou}_{j,t} + P^{ps}_{j,t}·Λ^{lem}_{j,t} + P^{gs}_{j,t}·Λ^{fit}_{t}) τ; P^{ps}_{j,t}, P^{gs}_{j,t} ≤ 0, ∀j∈J,∀t∈T, subject to: (29)−(35), (28) where the first and second terms in (28) refer to the total cost of buying energy from the peers and the upstream grid, respectively and the third and fourth terms define the total profit of selling energy to the peers and the upstream grid in the LEM, respectively. Here, P^{pb}_{j,t}/P^{ps}_{j,t} and P^{gb}_{j,t}/P^{gs}_{j,t} are buying/selling quantities of prosumer j with the peers and the upstream grid in each τ, respectively; and Λ^{tou}_{j,t} are the time-of-use (ToU) buying prices with the upstream grid."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E33","location":{"location_id":"src-1fe7e180ad-p08-c1r1__v141-a-M03-matching","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"P2P Trading Mechanism","anchor_text":"HOQUE et al.: DOE-BASED LEM FOR PROSUMERS WITH EVs by prosumer j ∈J from (to) prosumer i ∈J |i̸ = j.","equation_id":"(36)-(37)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The single P2P buying energy P^{pb}_{j,i,t} is limited by P^{pb}_{j,t} and the single P2P selling energy P^{ps}_{j,i,t} is constrained by P^{ps}_{j,t} as in (36) and (37), respectively, where P^{pb}_{j,t}/P^{ps}_{j,t} is the buying/selling quantity bid of prosumer j at a time t as in Section V-B. Prosumer j can only trade energy with prosumer i at time t as stated in (36) and (37), where C_{j,i,t} is a binary variable to represent the P2P trading status such that C_{j,i,t} = 1 if prosumer j buys energy from prosumer i. 0 ≤ P^{pb}_{j,i,t} ≤ P^{pb}_{j,t} C_{j,i,t}; ∀(j,i) ∈ J | j ≠ i, ∀t∈T, (36) P^{ps}_{j,t}(1 − C_{j,i,t}) ≤ P^{ps}_{j,i,t} ≤ 0; ∀(j,i) ∈ J | j ≠ i, ∀t∈T. (37)","paper":"43-operating_envelope_ev_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R006","quote":"The single P2P buying energy P^{pb}_{j,i,t} is limited by P^{pb}_{j,t} and the single P2P selling energy P^{ps}_{j,i,t} is constrained by P^{ps}_{j,t} as in (36) and (37), respectively, where P^{pb}_{j,t}/P^{ps}_{j,t} is the buying/selling quantity bid of prosumer j at a time t as in Section V-B. Prosumer j can only trade energy with prosumer i at time t as stated in (36) and (37), where C_{j,i,t} is a binary variable to represent the P2P trading status such that C_{j,i,t} = 1 if prosumer j buys energy from prosumer i. 0 ≤ P^{pb}_{j,i,t} ≤ P^{pb}_{j,t} C_{j,i,t}; ∀(j,i) ∈ J | j ≠ i, ∀t∈T, (36) P^{ps}_{j,t}(1 − C_{j,i,t}) ≤ P^{ps}_{j,i,t} ≤ 0; ∀(j,i) ∈ J | j ≠ i, ∀t∈T. (37)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E12","location":{"location_id":"src-1fe7e180ad-p04-c2r3__v141-a-M03-matching","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"Overview of the Proposed Framework","anchor_text":"unt Fig. 1. The proposed framework of DOE-based prosumers management in the LEM. ed ith consumption ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Finally, a P2P trading process is executed by a local market operator (LMO) through a matching mechanism to obtain the P2P clearing prices and the quantities of the trading energy with the peers (Step 9).","paper":"43-operating_envelope_ev_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R006","quote":"Finally, a P2P trading process is executed by a local market operator (LMO) through a matching mechanism to obtain the P2P clearing prices and the quantities of the trading energy with the peers (Step 9)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-e014","location":{"location_id":"src-1fe7e180ad-p10-c2r4__v141-a-M03-clearing","page":10,"printed_page":"1721","section":"P2P Trading Analysis","anchor_text":"g- for trading with the P2P and the upstream grid of a sample ed prosumer (j = 27). Results in Fig. ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 12","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-10.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"As explained earlier, prosumers generate their trading bids ($P_{j,i,t}^{pb}/P_{i,j,t}^{ps}$) and prices ($\\lambda_{j,i,t}^{c}$) optimally for the P2P trading coordinated by LMO in the proposed framework. Fig. 12 illustrates the P2P trading results of prosumers (buyers and sellers) at an arbitrarily-chosen sample time $t=39$.","paper":"43-operating_envelope_ev_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R006","quote":"As explained earlier, prosumers generate their trading bids ($P_{j,i,t}^{pb}/P_{i,j,t}^{ps}$) and prices ($\\lambda_{j,i,t}^{c}$) optimally for the P2P trading coordinated by LMO in the proposed framework. Fig. 12 illustrates the P2P trading results of prosumers (buyers and sellers) at an arbitrarily-chosen sample time $t=39$."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-e013","location":{"location_id":"src-1fe7e180ad-p11-c1r3__v141-a-M03-matching","page":11,"printed_page":"1722","section":"P2P Trading Analysis","anchor_text":"(¢) corresponding to those tradings are shown in Fig. 12b. As is noticed in Fig. 12, each P2P tradin","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 12","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-11.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"As is noticed in Fig. 12, each P2P trading is executed in a decentralized way, whereby a prosumer acting as a buyer purchases from another prosumer (who plays the role of a seller) at an optimal P2P trading price. Further, a buyer trades with multiple sellers simultaneously and vice versa is also true for a seller in order to meet the required energy quantity ($P_{j,t}^{pb}/P_{j,t}^{ps}$), where tradings are confined by the availability of their buying/selling amounts and constraints. Fig. 12 demonstrates that prosumers are able to manage their P2P tradings optimally by achieving their P2P trading limits and respecting both network and local market constraints.","paper":"43-operating_envelope_ev_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R006","quote":"As is noticed in Fig. 12, each P2P trading is executed in a decentralized way, whereby a prosumer acting as a buyer purchases from another prosumer (who plays the role of a seller) at an optimal P2P trading price. Further, a buyer trades with multiple sellers simultaneously and vice versa is also true for a seller in order to meet the required energy quantity ($P_{j,t}^{pb}/P_{j,t}^{ps}$), where tradings are confined by the availability of their buying/selling amounts and constraints. Fig. 12 demonstrates that prosumers are able to manage their P2P tradings optimally by achieving their P2P trading limits and respecting both network and local market constraints."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E28","location":{"location_id":"src-1fe7e180ad-p07-c2r2__v141-a-M03-bidding","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"Prosumers Bidding Strategy","anchor_text":"p y , j,t j,t j,t j,t y g g quantities of prosumer j with the peers and the upstream grid Vs- in eac","equation_id":"(29)-(30)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"Prosumers are allowed to trade in the LEM within the assigned DOEs P̂_{j,t} confirming the network-constrained operation. The sum of the buying energy of prosumer j at time t with the peers and the upstream grid should be equal to or less than the DOE limits P̂_{j,t}(> 0), and the sum of the selling energy with the peers and the upstream grid should be equal to or greater than the DOE limits P̂_{j,t}(≤ 0) as in (29) and (30), respectively. P^{pb}_{j,t} + P^{gb}_{j,t} ≤ P̂_{j,t}, if P̂_{j,t} > 0; ∀j∈J,∀t∈T, (29) P^{ps}_{j,t} + P^{gs}_{j,t} ≥ P̂_{j,t}, if P̂_{j,t} ≤ 0; ∀j∈J,∀t∈T. (30)","paper":"43-operating_envelope_ev_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R006","quote":"Prosumers are allowed to trade in the LEM within the assigned DOEs P̂_{j,t} confirming the network-constrained operation. The sum of the buying energy of prosumer j at time t with the peers and the upstream grid should be equal to or less than the DOE limits P̂_{j,t}(> 0), and the sum of the selling energy with the peers and the upstream grid should be equal to or greater than the DOE limits P̂_{j,t}(≤ 0) as in (29) and (30), respectively. P^{pb}_{j,t} + P^{gb}_{j,t} ≤ P̂_{j,t}, if P̂_{j,t} > 0; ∀j∈J,∀t∈T, (29) P^{ps}_{j,t} + P^{gs}_{j,t} ≥ P̂_{j,t}, if P̂_{j,t} ≤ 0; ∀j∈J,∀t∈T. (30)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E29","location":{"location_id":"src-1fe7e180ad-p07-c2r3__v141-a-M03-bidding","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"Prosumers Bidding Strategy","anchor_text":"1, in each τ is constrained by (31), which is not greater than 6), Pj,t(> 0), and the total P2P sell","equation_id":"(31)-(32)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"The total P2P buying quantity P^{pb}_{j,t}(> 0) for each prosumer in each τ is constrained by (31), which is not greater than P̂_{j,t}(> 0), and the total P2P selling quantity P^{ps}_{j,t}(\u003c 0) for each prosumer in each τ is limited by P̂_{j,t}(≤ 0) as in (32). 0 ≤ P^{pb}_{j,t} ≤ P̂_{j,t}, if P̂_{j,t} > 0; ∀j∈J,∀t∈T, (31) P̂_{j,t} ≤ P^{ps}_{j,t} ≤ 0, if P̂_{j,t} ≤ 0; ∀j∈J,∀t∈T. (32)","paper":"43-operating_envelope_ev_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R006","quote":"The total P2P buying quantity P^{pb}_{j,t}(> 0) for each prosumer in each τ is constrained by (31), which is not greater than P̂_{j,t}(> 0), and the total P2P selling quantity P^{ps}_{j,t}(\u003c 0) for each prosumer in each τ is limited by P̂_{j,t}(≤ 0) as in (32). 0 ≤ P^{pb}_{j,t} ≤ P̂_{j,t}, if P̂_{j,t} > 0; ∀j∈J,∀t∈T, (31) P̂_{j,t} ≤ P^{ps}_{j,t} ≤ 0, if P̂_{j,t} ≤ 0; ∀j∈J,∀t∈T. (32)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E30","location":{"location_id":"src-1fe7e180ad-p07-c2r3__v141-a-M03-bidding","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"Prosumers Bidding Strategy","anchor_text":"1, in each τ is constrained by (31), which is not greater than 6), Pj,t(> 0), and the total P2P sell","equation_id":"(33)-(34)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"On the other hand, constraints (33) and (34) limit the buying quantity P^{gb}_{j,t} and the selling quantity P^{gs}_{j,t} in each τ with the upstream grid, respectively. It is assumed that if no P2P trade occurs, the trade with the grid should be equal to the DOE but it is less than the DOE when there is a P2P trade. 0 ≤ P^{gb}_{j,t} ≤ P̂_{j,t}, if P̂_{j,t} > 0; ∀j∈J,∀t∈T, (33) P̂_{j,t} ≤ P^{gs}_{j,t} ≤ 0, if P̂_{j,t} ≤ 0; ∀j∈J,∀t∈T. (34)","paper":"43-operating_envelope_ev_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R006","quote":"On the other hand, constraints (33) and (34) limit the buying quantity P^{gb}_{j,t} and the selling quantity P^{gs}_{j,t} in each τ with the upstream grid, respectively. It is assumed that if no P2P trade occurs, the trade with the grid should be equal to the DOE but it is less than the DOE when there is a P2P trade. 0 ≤ P^{gb}_{j,t} ≤ P̂_{j,t}, if P̂_{j,t} > 0; ∀j∈J,∀t∈T, (33) P̂_{j,t} ≤ P^{gs}_{j,t} ≤ 0, if P̂_{j,t} ≤ 0; ∀j∈J,∀t∈T. (34)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E31","location":{"location_id":"src-1fe7e180ad-p07-c2r4__v141-a-M03-clearing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"P2P Trading Mechanism","anchor_text":"and the total selling of the P2P trading in each τ so that the re remaining amounts of imports/expor","equation_id":"(35)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Constraint (35) defines the power balance of the total buying and the total selling of the P2P trading in each τ so that the remaining amounts of imports/exports of prosumers within P̂_{j,t} can be traded with the upstream grid in the LEM. ∑_{j∈J} P^{pb}_{j,t} + ∑_{j∈J} P^{ps}_{j,t} = 0; P^{ps}_{j,t} ≤ 0, ∀t∈T. (35)","paper":"43-operating_envelope_ev_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R006","quote":"Constraint (35) defines the power balance of the total buying and the total selling of the P2P trading in each τ so that the remaining amounts of imports/exports of prosumers within P̂_{j,t} can be traded with the upstream grid in the LEM. ∑_{j∈J} P^{pb}_{j,t} + ∑_{j∈J} P^{ps}_{j,t} = 0; P^{ps}_{j,t} ≤ 0, ∀t∈T. (35)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E34","location":{"location_id":"src-1fe7e180ad-p08-c1r2__v141-a-M03-matching","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"P2P Trading Mechanism","anchor_text":"0 ≤Ppbj,i,t ≤Ppbj,t Cj,i,t; ∀(j, i) ∈J |j̸ = i, ∀t ∈T , (36) Ppsj,t 1 −Cj,i,t ≤Ppsj,i,t ≤0; ∀(j, i) ","equation_id":"(38)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Equation (38) refers to the energy matching constraint of prosumers' buying and selling in each P2P trade at time t, which implies that the amount of buying energy by prosumer j from prosumer i should be equal to the amount of selling energy by prosumer i to prosumer j at time t. P^{pb}_{j,i,t} + P^{ps}_{i,j,t} = 0; P^{ps}_{i,j,t} ≤ 0, ∀(j,i) ∈ J | i ≠ j, ∀t∈T. (38)","paper":"43-operating_envelope_ev_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R006","quote":"Equation (38) refers to the energy matching constraint of prosumers' buying and selling in each P2P trade at time t, which implies that the amount of buying energy by prosumer j from prosumer i should be equal to the amount of selling energy by prosumer i to prosumer j at time t. P^{pb}_{j,i,t} + P^{ps}_{i,j,t} = 0; P^{ps}_{i,j,t} ≤ 0, ∀(j,i) ∈ J | i ≠ j, ∀t∈T. (38)"}],"candidate_only":true,"classification_subtypes":["peer_trade_execution_and_grid_interface"],"projection_statuses":["clear"],"taxonomy":{"primary_family":"kind-L7-1cdb7b7e84","secondary_families":[],"stage":"L7","ontological_kind":"peer_trade_execution_and_grid_interface"},"semantic_definition":{},"source_units":[{"unit_id":"43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-a-M03-lem::execution.energy_trade","paper_id":"43-operating_envelope_ev_market","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M03-lem","function":"execution.energy_trade","source_occurrences":[{"id":"43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R006::V::execution.energy_trade","rule_id":"v141-c-R006","market_meaning":"The submitted total P2P buying-quantity bid limits each individual P2P purchase through the upper bound P^{pb}_{j,t} C_{j,i,t}. Scope: Individual P2P purchases by prosumer j from a different prosumer i at each time t. Condition: Subject to the trading-status factor C_{j,i,t} in (36). The submitted total P2P selling-quantity bid limits each individual P2P sale through the signed lower bound P^{ps}_{j,t}(1 − C_{j,i,t}). Scope: Individual P2P sales by prosumer j to a different prosumer i at each time t. Condition: Subject to the complementary trading-status factor 1 − C_{j,i,t} in (37); selling quantities are nonpositive. The local market operator executes and coordinates P2P trading among prosumers. Scope: The proposed LEM's P2P trading process, including Step 9. The optimal P2P trading price applies to the executed exchange between a buyer and a seller. Scope: P2P exchanges reported in Fig. 12 at the sample time t=39. Combined peer and upstream-grid purchases must not exceed the assigned import DOE. Each peer and grid buying quantity is nonnegative and individually bounded by that DOE. Scope: Prosumer purchases from peers and the upstream grid in each time-slot. Condition: The assigned DOE P̂_{j,t} is positive. Combined signed peer and upstream-grid sales must be at or above the assigned export DOE. Each peer and grid selling quantity lies between that DOE and zero. Scope: Prosumer sales to peers and the upstream grid in each time-slot, using nonpositive signed selling quantities. Condition: The assigned DOE P̂_{j,t} is nonpositive. Total P2P buying and total P2P selling must balance in each time-slot. Scope: Aggregate P2P trading in each time-slot τ. The amount bought by j from i must equal the amount sold by i to j in the same trade and time-slot. Scope: Each individual P2P trade between distinct prosumers j and i at time t. Remaining imports or exports may be traded with the upstream grid. Scope: Residual upstream-grid exchanges included in the LEM. Condition: Imports or exports remain after P2P trading and are within the assigned DOE P̂_{j,t}. The strategy assumes that the grid trade equals the assigned DOE. Scope: Upstream-grid trading included in the proposed LEM strategy. Condition: No P2P trade occurs.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"activation","context_text":"Aggregate P2P trading in each time-slot τ. | Each individual P2P trade between distinct prosumers j and i at time t. | Individual P2P purchases by prosumer j from a different prosumer i at each time t. | Individual P2P sales by prosumer j to a different prosumer i at each time t. | P2P exchanges reported in Fig. 12 at the sample time t=39. | Prosumer purchases from peers and the upstream grid in each time-slot. | Prosumer sales to peers and the upstream grid in each time-slot, using nonpositive signed selling quantities. | Residual upstream-grid exchanges included in the LEM. | The proposed LEM's P2P trading process, including Step 9. | Upstream-grid trading included in the proposed LEM strategy.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g02-E27","v141-b-g02-E28","v141-b-g02-E29","v141-b-g02-E30","v141-b-g02-E31","v141-b-g02-E33","v141-b-g02-E34","v141-b-g03-e013","v141-b-g03-e014"]},"constraint_refs":["43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C001","43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C002","43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C003","43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C004","43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C005","43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C006","43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C007","43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C008","43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C009","43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C010"],"decision_anchor":"execution.energy_trade","source_rule_sha256":"6f886284b421760a203dcd266e69537ae7b3451952fb1d55cbec933b14f8be6f"}],"constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C001","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The submitted total P2P buying-quantity bid limits each individual P2P purchase through the upper bound P^{pb}_{j,t} C_{j,i,t}. Scope: Individual P2P purchases by prosumer j from a different prosumer i at each time t. Condition: Subject to the trading-status factor C_{j,i,t} in (36).","expression":"0 \\le P^{pb}_{j,i,t} \\le P^{pb}_{j,t} C_{j,i,t};\\quad C_{j,i,t}\\in\\{0,1\\};\\quad \\forall (j,i)\\in J\\mid j\\ne i,\\ \\forall t\\in T. (36)","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.demand","execution.energy_trade"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R006-X001","v141-c-R006-X003","v141-c-R006-X005"],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E27","v141-b-g02-E33"],"ref":"43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C001","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R006","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E27","location":{"location_id":"src-1fe7e180ad-p07-c2r1__v141-a-M03-bidding","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"Prosumers Bidding Strategy","anchor_text":"IEEE TRANSACTIONS ON SMART GRID, VOL. 15, NO. 2, MARCH 2024 lem tou lem ad min Ppbj,t · j,t + Pgbj,t","equation_id":"(28)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Prosumers can decide on their participation in the P2P trading or trading with the upstream grid by generating their bids for buying/selling energy within DOEs. Each prosumer decides on the trading bids and submits them to the LEM in each τ by the proposed bidding strategy. In this case, the objective of prosumer is to minimize the total trading cost as, min ∑_{j∈J} (P^{pb}_{j,t}·Λ^{lem}_{j,t} + P^{gb}_{j,t}·Λ^{tou}_{j,t} + P^{ps}_{j,t}·Λ^{lem}_{j,t} + P^{gs}_{j,t}·Λ^{fit}_{t}) τ; P^{ps}_{j,t}, P^{gs}_{j,t} ≤ 0, ∀j∈J,∀t∈T, subject to: (29)−(35), (28) where the first and second terms in (28) refer to the total cost of buying energy from the peers and the upstream grid, respectively and the third and fourth terms define the total profit of selling energy to the peers and the upstream grid in the LEM, respectively. Here, P^{pb}_{j,t}/P^{ps}_{j,t} and P^{gb}_{j,t}/P^{gs}_{j,t} are buying/selling quantities of prosumer j with the peers and the upstream grid in each τ, respectively; and Λ^{tou}_{j,t} are the time-of-use (ToU) buying prices with the upstream grid."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E33","location":{"location_id":"src-1fe7e180ad-p08-c1r1__v141-a-M03-matching","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"P2P Trading Mechanism","anchor_text":"HOQUE et al.: DOE-BASED LEM FOR PROSUMERS WITH EVs by prosumer j ∈J from (to) prosumer i ∈J |i̸ = j.","equation_id":"(36)-(37)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The single P2P buying energy P^{pb}_{j,i,t} is limited by P^{pb}_{j,t} and the single P2P selling energy P^{ps}_{j,i,t} is constrained by P^{ps}_{j,t} as in (36) and (37), respectively, where P^{pb}_{j,t}/P^{ps}_{j,t} is the buying/selling quantity bid of prosumer j at a time t as in Section V-B. Prosumer j can only trade energy with prosumer i at time t as stated in (36) and (37), where C_{j,i,t} is a binary variable to represent the P2P trading status such that C_{j,i,t} = 1 if prosumer j buys energy from prosumer i. 0 ≤ P^{pb}_{j,i,t} ≤ P^{pb}_{j,t} C_{j,i,t}; ∀(j,i) ∈ J | j ≠ i, ∀t∈T, (36) P^{ps}_{j,t}(1 − C_{j,i,t}) ≤ P^{ps}_{j,i,t} ≤ 0; ∀(j,i) ∈ J | j ≠ i, ∀t∈T. (37)"}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C002","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The submitted total P2P selling-quantity bid limits each individual P2P sale through the signed lower bound P^{ps}_{j,t}(1 − C_{j,i,t}). Scope: Individual P2P sales by prosumer j to a different prosumer i at each time t. Condition: Subject to the complementary trading-status factor 1 − C_{j,i,t} in (37); selling quantities are nonpositive.","expression":"P^{ps}_{j,t}(1 - C_{j,i,t}) \\le P^{ps}_{j,i,t} \\le 0;\\quad C_{j,i,t}\\in\\{0,1\\};\\quad \\forall (j,i)\\in J\\mid j\\ne i,\\ \\forall t\\in T. (37)","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply","execution.energy_trade"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R006-X002","v141-c-R006-X004","v141-c-R006-X005"],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E27","v141-b-g02-E33"],"ref":"43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C002","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R006","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E27","location":{"location_id":"src-1fe7e180ad-p07-c2r1__v141-a-M03-bidding","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"Prosumers Bidding Strategy","anchor_text":"IEEE TRANSACTIONS ON SMART GRID, VOL. 15, NO. 2, MARCH 2024 lem tou lem ad min Ppbj,t · j,t + Pgbj,t","equation_id":"(28)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Prosumers can decide on their participation in the P2P trading or trading with the upstream grid by generating their bids for buying/selling energy within DOEs. Each prosumer decides on the trading bids and submits them to the LEM in each τ by the proposed bidding strategy. In this case, the objective of prosumer is to minimize the total trading cost as, min ∑_{j∈J} (P^{pb}_{j,t}·Λ^{lem}_{j,t} + P^{gb}_{j,t}·Λ^{tou}_{j,t} + P^{ps}_{j,t}·Λ^{lem}_{j,t} + P^{gs}_{j,t}·Λ^{fit}_{t}) τ; P^{ps}_{j,t}, P^{gs}_{j,t} ≤ 0, ∀j∈J,∀t∈T, subject to: (29)−(35), (28) where the first and second terms in (28) refer to the total cost of buying energy from the peers and the upstream grid, respectively and the third and fourth terms define the total profit of selling energy to the peers and the upstream grid in the LEM, respectively. Here, P^{pb}_{j,t}/P^{ps}_{j,t} and P^{gb}_{j,t}/P^{gs}_{j,t} are buying/selling quantities of prosumer j with the peers and the upstream grid in each τ, respectively; and Λ^{tou}_{j,t} are the time-of-use (ToU) buying prices with the upstream grid."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E33","location":{"location_id":"src-1fe7e180ad-p08-c1r1__v141-a-M03-matching","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"P2P Trading Mechanism","anchor_text":"HOQUE et al.: DOE-BASED LEM FOR PROSUMERS WITH EVs by prosumer j ∈J from (to) prosumer i ∈J |i̸ = j.","equation_id":"(36)-(37)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The single P2P buying energy P^{pb}_{j,i,t} is limited by P^{pb}_{j,t} and the single P2P selling energy P^{ps}_{j,i,t} is constrained by P^{ps}_{j,t} as in (36) and (37), respectively, where P^{pb}_{j,t}/P^{ps}_{j,t} is the buying/selling quantity bid of prosumer j at a time t as in Section V-B. Prosumer j can only trade energy with prosumer i at time t as stated in (36) and (37), where C_{j,i,t} is a binary variable to represent the P2P trading status such that C_{j,i,t} = 1 if prosumer j buys energy from prosumer i. 0 ≤ P^{pb}_{j,i,t} ≤ P^{pb}_{j,t} C_{j,i,t}; ∀(j,i) ∈ J | j ≠ i, ∀t∈T, (36) P^{ps}_{j,t}(1 − C_{j,i,t}) ≤ P^{ps}_{j,i,t} ≤ 0; ∀(j,i) ∈ J | j ≠ i, ∀t∈T. (37)"}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The local market operator executes and coordinates P2P trading among prosumers. Scope: The proposed LEM's P2P trading process, including Step 9.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","execution.energy_trade"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g03-e014"],"ref":"43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C003","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R006","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E12","location":{"location_id":"src-1fe7e180ad-p04-c2r3__v141-a-M03-matching","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"Overview of the Proposed Framework","anchor_text":"unt Fig. 1. The proposed framework of DOE-based prosumers management in the LEM. ed ith consumption ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Finally, a P2P trading process is executed by a local market operator (LMO) through a matching mechanism to obtain the P2P clearing prices and the quantities of the trading energy with the peers (Step 9)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-e014","location":{"location_id":"src-1fe7e180ad-p10-c2r4__v141-a-M03-clearing","page":10,"printed_page":"1721","section":"P2P Trading Analysis","anchor_text":"g- for trading with the P2P and the upstream grid of a sample ed prosumer (j = 27). Results in Fig. ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 12","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-10.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"As explained earlier, prosumers generate their trading bids ($P_{j,i,t}^{pb}/P_{i,j,t}^{ps}$) and prices ($\\lambda_{j,i,t}^{c}$) optimally for the P2P trading coordinated by LMO in the proposed framework. Fig. 12 illustrates the P2P trading results of prosumers (buyers and sellers) at an arbitrarily-chosen sample time $t=39$."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C004","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The optimal P2P trading price applies to the executed exchange between a buyer and a seller. Scope: P2P exchanges reported in Fig. 12 at the sample time t=39.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","execution.energy_trade"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g03-e013","v141-b-g03-e014"],"ref":"43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C004","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R006","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E12","location":{"location_id":"src-1fe7e180ad-p04-c2r3__v141-a-M03-matching","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"Overview of the Proposed Framework","anchor_text":"unt Fig. 1. The proposed framework of DOE-based prosumers management in the LEM. ed ith consumption ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Finally, a P2P trading process is executed by a local market operator (LMO) through a matching mechanism to obtain the P2P clearing prices and the quantities of the trading energy with the peers (Step 9)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-e013","location":{"location_id":"src-1fe7e180ad-p11-c1r3__v141-a-M03-matching","page":11,"printed_page":"1722","section":"P2P Trading Analysis","anchor_text":"(¢) corresponding to those tradings are shown in Fig. 12b. As is noticed in Fig. 12, each P2P tradin","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 12","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-11.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"As is noticed in Fig. 12, each P2P trading is executed in a decentralized way, whereby a prosumer acting as a buyer purchases from another prosumer (who plays the role of a seller) at an optimal P2P trading price. Further, a buyer trades with multiple sellers simultaneously and vice versa is also true for a seller in order to meet the required energy quantity ($P_{j,t}^{pb}/P_{j,t}^{ps}$), where tradings are confined by the availability of their buying/selling amounts and constraints. Fig. 12 demonstrates that prosumers are able to manage their P2P tradings optimally by achieving their P2P trading limits and respecting both network and local market constraints."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-e014","location":{"location_id":"src-1fe7e180ad-p10-c2r4__v141-a-M03-clearing","page":10,"printed_page":"1721","section":"P2P Trading Analysis","anchor_text":"g- for trading with the P2P and the upstream grid of a sample ed prosumer (j = 27). Results in Fig. ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 12","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-10.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"As explained earlier, prosumers generate their trading bids ($P_{j,i,t}^{pb}/P_{i,j,t}^{ps}$) and prices ($\\lambda_{j,i,t}^{c}$) optimally for the P2P trading coordinated by LMO in the proposed framework. Fig. 12 illustrates the P2P trading results of prosumers (buyers and sellers) at an arbitrarily-chosen sample time $t=39$."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C005","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"Combined peer and upstream-grid purchases must not exceed the assigned import DOE. Each peer and grid buying quantity is nonnegative and individually bounded by that DOE. Scope: Prosumer purchases from peers and the upstream grid in each time-slot. Condition: The assigned DOE P̂_{j,t} is positive.","expression":"P^{pb}_{j,t}+P^{gb}_{j,t}\\le \\hat{P}_{j,t};\\quad 0\\le P^{pb}_{j,t}\\le \\hat{P}_{j,t};\\quad 0\\le P^{gb}_{j,t}\\le \\hat{P}_{j,t};\\quad \\text{if }\\hat{P}_{j,t}>0;\\quad \\forall j\\in J,\\ \\forall t\\in T. (29),(31),(33)","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["execution.energy_trade"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R006-X001","v141-c-R006-X006"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R006-T001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E28","v141-b-g02-E29","v141-b-g02-E30"],"ref":"43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C005","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R006","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E28","location":{"location_id":"src-1fe7e180ad-p07-c2r2__v141-a-M03-bidding","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"Prosumers Bidding Strategy","anchor_text":"p y , j,t j,t j,t j,t y g g quantities of prosumer j with the peers and the upstream grid Vs- in eac","equation_id":"(29)-(30)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"Prosumers are allowed to trade in the LEM within the assigned DOEs P̂_{j,t} confirming the network-constrained operation. The sum of the buying energy of prosumer j at time t with the peers and the upstream grid should be equal to or less than the DOE limits P̂_{j,t}(> 0), and the sum of the selling energy with the peers and the upstream grid should be equal to or greater than the DOE limits P̂_{j,t}(≤ 0) as in (29) and (30), respectively. P^{pb}_{j,t} + P^{gb}_{j,t} ≤ P̂_{j,t}, if P̂_{j,t} > 0; ∀j∈J,∀t∈T, (29) P^{ps}_{j,t} + P^{gs}_{j,t} ≥ P̂_{j,t}, if P̂_{j,t} ≤ 0; ∀j∈J,∀t∈T. (30)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E29","location":{"location_id":"src-1fe7e180ad-p07-c2r3__v141-a-M03-bidding","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"Prosumers Bidding Strategy","anchor_text":"1, in each τ is constrained by (31), which is not greater than 6), Pj,t(> 0), and the total P2P sell","equation_id":"(31)-(32)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"The total P2P buying quantity P^{pb}_{j,t}(> 0) for each prosumer in each τ is constrained by (31), which is not greater than P̂_{j,t}(> 0), and the total P2P selling quantity P^{ps}_{j,t}(\u003c 0) for each prosumer in each τ is limited by P̂_{j,t}(≤ 0) as in (32). 0 ≤ P^{pb}_{j,t} ≤ P̂_{j,t}, if P̂_{j,t} > 0; ∀j∈J,∀t∈T, (31) P̂_{j,t} ≤ P^{ps}_{j,t} ≤ 0, if P̂_{j,t} ≤ 0; ∀j∈J,∀t∈T. (32)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E30","location":{"location_id":"src-1fe7e180ad-p07-c2r3__v141-a-M03-bidding","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"Prosumers Bidding Strategy","anchor_text":"1, in each τ is constrained by (31), which is not greater than 6), Pj,t(> 0), and the total P2P sell","equation_id":"(33)-(34)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"On the other hand, constraints (33) and (34) limit the buying quantity P^{gb}_{j,t} and the selling quantity P^{gs}_{j,t} in each τ with the upstream grid, respectively. It is assumed that if no P2P trade occurs, the trade with the grid should be equal to the DOE but it is less than the DOE when there is a P2P trade. 0 ≤ P^{gb}_{j,t} ≤ P̂_{j,t}, if P̂_{j,t} > 0; ∀j∈J,∀t∈T, (33) P̂_{j,t} ≤ P^{gs}_{j,t} ≤ 0, if P̂_{j,t} ≤ 0; ∀j∈J,∀t∈T. (34)"}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C006","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"Combined signed peer and upstream-grid sales must be at or above the assigned export DOE. Each peer and grid selling quantity lies between that DOE and zero. Scope: Prosumer sales to peers and the upstream grid in each time-slot, using nonpositive signed selling quantities. Condition: The assigned DOE P̂_{j,t} is nonpositive.","expression":"P^{ps}_{j,t}+P^{gs}_{j,t}\\ge \\hat{P}_{j,t};\\quad \\hat{P}_{j,t}\\le P^{ps}_{j,t}\\le 0;\\quad \\hat{P}_{j,t}\\le P^{gs}_{j,t}\\le 0;\\quad \\text{if }\\hat{P}_{j,t}\\le 0;\\quad \\forall j\\in J,\\ \\forall t\\in T. (30),(32),(34)","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["execution.energy_trade"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R006-X002","v141-c-R006-X007"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R006-T001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E28","v141-b-g02-E29","v141-b-g02-E30"],"ref":"43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C006","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R006","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E28","location":{"location_id":"src-1fe7e180ad-p07-c2r2__v141-a-M03-bidding","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"Prosumers Bidding Strategy","anchor_text":"p y , j,t j,t j,t j,t y g g quantities of prosumer j with the peers and the upstream grid Vs- in eac","equation_id":"(29)-(30)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"Prosumers are allowed to trade in the LEM within the assigned DOEs P̂_{j,t} confirming the network-constrained operation. The sum of the buying energy of prosumer j at time t with the peers and the upstream grid should be equal to or less than the DOE limits P̂_{j,t}(> 0), and the sum of the selling energy with the peers and the upstream grid should be equal to or greater than the DOE limits P̂_{j,t}(≤ 0) as in (29) and (30), respectively. P^{pb}_{j,t} + P^{gb}_{j,t} ≤ P̂_{j,t}, if P̂_{j,t} > 0; ∀j∈J,∀t∈T, (29) P^{ps}_{j,t} + P^{gs}_{j,t} ≥ P̂_{j,t}, if P̂_{j,t} ≤ 0; ∀j∈J,∀t∈T. (30)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E29","location":{"location_id":"src-1fe7e180ad-p07-c2r3__v141-a-M03-bidding","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"Prosumers Bidding Strategy","anchor_text":"1, in each τ is constrained by (31), which is not greater than 6), Pj,t(> 0), and the total P2P sell","equation_id":"(31)-(32)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"The total P2P buying quantity P^{pb}_{j,t}(> 0) for each prosumer in each τ is constrained by (31), which is not greater than P̂_{j,t}(> 0), and the total P2P selling quantity P^{ps}_{j,t}(\u003c 0) for each prosumer in each τ is limited by P̂_{j,t}(≤ 0) as in (32). 0 ≤ P^{pb}_{j,t} ≤ P̂_{j,t}, if P̂_{j,t} > 0; ∀j∈J,∀t∈T, (31) P̂_{j,t} ≤ P^{ps}_{j,t} ≤ 0, if P̂_{j,t} ≤ 0; ∀j∈J,∀t∈T. (32)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E30","location":{"location_id":"src-1fe7e180ad-p07-c2r3__v141-a-M03-bidding","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"Prosumers Bidding Strategy","anchor_text":"1, in each τ is constrained by (31), which is not greater than 6), Pj,t(> 0), and the total P2P sell","equation_id":"(33)-(34)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"On the other hand, constraints (33) and (34) limit the buying quantity P^{gb}_{j,t} and the selling quantity P^{gs}_{j,t} in each τ with the upstream grid, respectively. It is assumed that if no P2P trade occurs, the trade with the grid should be equal to the DOE but it is less than the DOE when there is a P2P trade. 0 ≤ P^{gb}_{j,t} ≤ P̂_{j,t}, if P̂_{j,t} > 0; ∀j∈J,∀t∈T, (33) P̂_{j,t} ≤ P^{gs}_{j,t} ≤ 0, if P̂_{j,t} ≤ 0; ∀j∈J,∀t∈T. (34)"}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C007","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"Total P2P buying and total P2P selling must balance in each time-slot. Scope: Aggregate P2P trading in each time-slot τ.","expression":"\\sum_{j\\in J} P^{pb}_{j,t}+\\sum_{j\\in J} P^{ps}_{j,t}=0;\\quad P^{ps}_{j,t}\\le 0,\\quad \\forall t\\in T. (35)","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["execution.energy_trade"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R006-X001","v141-c-R006-X002"],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E31"],"ref":"43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C007","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R006","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E31","location":{"location_id":"src-1fe7e180ad-p07-c2r4__v141-a-M03-clearing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"P2P Trading Mechanism","anchor_text":"and the total selling of the P2P trading in each τ so that the re remaining amounts of imports/expor","equation_id":"(35)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Constraint (35) defines the power balance of the total buying and the total selling of the P2P trading in each τ so that the remaining amounts of imports/exports of prosumers within P̂_{j,t} can be traded with the upstream grid in the LEM. ∑_{j∈J} P^{pb}_{j,t} + ∑_{j∈J} P^{ps}_{j,t} = 0; P^{ps}_{j,t} ≤ 0, ∀t∈T. (35)"}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C008","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The amount bought by j from i must equal the amount sold by i to j in the same trade and time-slot. Scope: Each individual P2P trade between distinct prosumers j and i at time t.","expression":"P^{pb}_{j,i,t}+P^{ps}_{i,j,t}=0;\\quad P^{ps}_{i,j,t}\\le 0,\\quad \\forall (j,i)\\in J\\mid i\\ne j,\\ \\forall t\\in T. (38)","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["execution.energy_trade"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R006-X003","v141-c-R006-X004"],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E34"],"ref":"43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C008","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R006","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E34","location":{"location_id":"src-1fe7e180ad-p08-c1r2__v141-a-M03-matching","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"P2P Trading Mechanism","anchor_text":"0 ≤Ppbj,i,t ≤Ppbj,t Cj,i,t; ∀(j, i) ∈J |j̸ = i, ∀t ∈T , (36) Ppsj,t 1 −Cj,i,t ≤Ppsj,i,t ≤0; ∀(j, i) ","equation_id":"(38)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Equation (38) refers to the energy matching constraint of prosumers' buying and selling in each P2P trade at time t, which implies that the amount of buying energy by prosumer j from prosumer i should be equal to the amount of selling energy by prosumer i to prosumer j at time t. P^{pb}_{j,i,t} + P^{ps}_{i,j,t} = 0; P^{ps}_{i,j,t} ≤ 0, ∀(j,i) ∈ J | i ≠ j, ∀t∈T. (38)"}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C009","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Remaining imports or exports may be traded with the upstream grid. Scope: Residual upstream-grid exchanges included in the LEM. Condition: Imports or exports remain after P2P trading and are within the assigned DOE P̂_{j,t}.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["execution.energy_trade"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E31"],"ref":"43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C009","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R006","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E31","location":{"location_id":"src-1fe7e180ad-p07-c2r4__v141-a-M03-clearing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"P2P Trading Mechanism","anchor_text":"and the total selling of the P2P trading in each τ so that the re remaining amounts of imports/expor","equation_id":"(35)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Constraint (35) defines the power balance of the total buying and the total selling of the P2P trading in each τ so that the remaining amounts of imports/exports of prosumers within P̂_{j,t} can be traded with the upstream grid in the LEM. ∑_{j∈J} P^{pb}_{j,t} + ∑_{j∈J} P^{ps}_{j,t} = 0; P^{ps}_{j,t} ≤ 0, ∀t∈T. (35)"}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C010","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The strategy assumes that the grid trade equals the assigned DOE. Scope: Upstream-grid trading included in the proposed LEM strategy. Condition: No P2P trade occurs.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["execution.energy_trade"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E30"],"ref":"43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C010","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R006","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E30","location":{"location_id":"src-1fe7e180ad-p07-c2r3__v141-a-M03-bidding","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"Prosumers Bidding Strategy","anchor_text":"1, in each τ is constrained by (31), which is not greater than 6), Pj,t(> 0), and the total P2P sell","equation_id":"(33)-(34)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"On the other hand, constraints (33) and (34) limit the buying quantity P^{gb}_{j,t} and the selling quantity P^{gs}_{j,t} in each τ with the upstream grid, respectively. It is assumed that if no P2P trade occurs, the trade with the grid should be equal to the DOE but it is less than the DOE when there is a P2P trade. 0 ≤ P^{gb}_{j,t} ≤ P̂_{j,t}, if P̂_{j,t} > 0; ∀j∈J,∀t∈T, (33) P̂_{j,t} ≤ P^{gs}_{j,t} ≤ 0, if P̂_{j,t} ≤ 0; ∀j∈J,∀t∈T. (34)"}]}],"variables":[{"variable_id":"v141-c-R006-X001","symbol":"P^{pb}_{j,t}","meaning":"Total P2P buying-quantity bid of prosumer j at time t, which limits the individual P2P purchase P^{pb}_{j,i,t}.","kind":"operational","domain":"Nonnegative real, bounded by 0 \u003c= P^{pb}_{j,t} \u003c= \\hat{P}_{j,t} when \\hat{P}_{j,t} > 0 (source eq. (31)); the source also calls it a buying-quantity bid as in Section V-B.","unit":null,"indices":["j","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E27","v141-b-g02-E29","v141-b-g02-E33"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R006","declaration_ref":"43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-X001"},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R006-X002","symbol":"P^{ps}_{j,t}","meaning":"Total signed P2P selling-quantity bid of prosumer j at time t, which constrains the individual P2P sale P^{ps}_{j,i,t}.","kind":"operational","domain":"Nonpositive real; bounded by \\hat{P}_{j,t} \u003c= P^{ps}_{j,t} \u003c= 0 when \\hat{P}_{j,t} \u003c= 0 (source eq. (32)); the source also states P^{ps}_{j,t} \u003c= 0 globally in (28).","unit":null,"indices":["j","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E27","v141-b-g02-E29","v141-b-g02-E33"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R006","declaration_ref":"43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-X002"},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R006-X003","symbol":"P^{pb}_{j,i,t}","meaning":"Individual P2P buying energy by prosumer j from a different prosumer i at time t.","kind":"operational","domain":"Nonnegative real per (36): 0 \u003c= P^{pb}_{j,i,t} \u003c= P^{pb}_{j,t} C_{j,i,t}.","unit":null,"indices":["j","i","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E33"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R006","declaration_ref":"43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-X003"},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R006-X004","symbol":"P^{ps}_{j,i,t}","meaning":"Signed individual P2P selling energy by prosumer j to a different prosumer i at time t; the source also writes P^{ps}_{i,j,t} for the reverse pair in (38).","kind":"operational","domain":"Nonpositive real per (37): P^{ps}_{j,t}(1 - C_{j,i,t}) \u003c= P^{ps}_{j,i,t} \u003c= 0.","unit":null,"indices":["j","i","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E33","v141-b-g02-E34"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R006","declaration_ref":"43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-X004"},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R006-X005","symbol":"C_{j,i,t}","meaning":"Binary P2P trading-status variable; C_{j,i,t} = 1 if prosumer j buys energy from prosumer i.","kind":"operational","domain":"{0,1} binary.","unit":null,"indices":["j","i","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E33"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R006","declaration_ref":"43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-X005"},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R006-X006","symbol":"P^{gb}_{j,t}","meaning":"Upstream-grid buying quantity of prosumer j at time t.","kind":"operational","domain":"Nonnegative real; 0 \u003c= P^{gb}_{j,t} \u003c= \\hat{P}_{j,t} when \\hat{P}_{j,t} > 0 (source eq. (33)).","unit":null,"indices":["j","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E27","v141-b-g02-E30"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R006","declaration_ref":"43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-X006"},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R006-X007","symbol":"P^{gs}_{j,t}","meaning":"Signed upstream-grid selling quantity of prosumer j at time t.","kind":"operational","domain":"Nonpositive real; \\hat{P}_{j,t} \u003c= P^{gs}_{j,t} \u003c= 0 when \\hat{P}_{j,t} \u003c= 0 (source eq. (34)).","unit":null,"indices":["j","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E27","v141-b-g02-E30"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R006","declaration_ref":"43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-X007"}],"parameters":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R006-T001","symbol":"\\hat{P}_{j,t}","meaning":"Assigned import/export DOE limit for prosumer j at time t; the positive branch bounds combined and individual purchases, and the nonpositive branch bounds combined and individual sales.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"assigned by the DOE computation; value not fixed in this rule"},"unit":null,"indices":["j","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E28","v141-b-g02-E29","v141-b-g02-E30"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R006","declaration_ref":"43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R006::theta::v141-c-R006-T001"}]}],"source_definitions":[{"unit_id":"43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-a-M03-lem::execution.energy_trade","stage":"L7","subtype":"peer_trade_execution_and_grid_interface","projection_status":"clear","target_definition":"Under LMO coordination, buyers and sellers conduct transactions according to the bilaterally optimized quantities and P2P prices; after P2P transactions, the remaining imports and exports may be traded with the upstream grid within the DOE. When there is no P2P transaction, the strategy assumes that the grid-side transaction quantity equals the allocated DOE.","form_kind":"procedural","identity_fields":["Object: bilateral P2P exchange and residual grid-side exchange","Core operation: execute buying and selling and connect the residual imports and exports to upstream trading","Output: bilateral exchange conducted according to quantity and price and conditional grid-side uptake"],"variation_fields":["Execution complies with quantity declaration, binary transaction status, and the DOE boundary","Import branch P̂>0, the purchased quantity is non-negative, and the combined peer and grid-side amount does not exceed P̂","Export branch P̂≤0, the sales quantity is non-positive, and the combined peer and grid-side amount is not less than P̂","The P2P aggregate balance and the pairwise P^{pb}_{j,i,t}+P^{ps}_{i,j,t}=0 are execution conditions","The example allows a buyer to trade simultaneously with multiple sellers, and vice versa","The equality of grid-side transactions to DOE when there is no P2P is a source assumption"],"constraint_refs":["43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C003","43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C004","43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C005","43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C006","43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C007","43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C008","43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C009","43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C010"],"paper_id":"43-operating_envelope_ev_market","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M03-lem","function":"execution.energy_trade","template_code":"BCT"}],"source_variants":[],"functional":{"is_child":false,"subdivision_pending":false},"canonical_pointer":"/nodes/212"});
